## Slide 1

Development of High Aspect Ratio Deep Reactive Ion Etching Using Design of Experiments

Mick Deines
University of Washington

## Slide 2

Reactive Ion Etching and the Bosch Process

Reactive Ion Etching (RIE) uses plasma and electromagnetic current to etch target material.
The Bosch process improves etch depth and sidewall verticality by alternating deposition and etching steps.

Figure 1: Diagrams of (a) standard RIE sidewall profile and (b) Bosch process RIE sidewall profile. Notice how the thin passivation layer protects the sidewalls and keeps them vertical.

## Slide 3

Aspect Ratio and Applications

The aspect ratio is the ratio of feature depth to feature width.
Maximizing aspect ratio is important for fabrication of MEMS devices.
One way to improve the aspect ratio is to lower the etch pressure.

Figure 2: Diagrams of (a) high pressure RIE sidewall profile and (b) low pressure RIE sidewall profile. Notice how higher pressures can lead to off-axis ions, leading to aspect ratio dependent etching.

## Slide 4

Methods

1 mm-thick, 100 mm silicon wafers
4 μm of SiO2 deposited via PECVD
7 μm of AZ10XT photoresist
Standard etch mask with trenches of widths varying from 5 μm to 500 μm

Figure 3: Silicon wafer patterned with standard etch mask

