## Slide 8

Conclusions and Future Work

This project led to a high aspect ratio Deep Reactive Ion Etching recipe for use at the Washington Nanofabrication Facility for our industrial and academic users.
Next steps:
New etch mask with 1 μm trenches
Thicker oxide layer to allow for longer etches
Recipe limit characterization
From this project, I became more familiar with dry etching processes and their mechanisms as well as using statistical tools to optimize a process. These skills are vital for helping me achieve my goals of becoming a process engineer.
 

